University Recommendations

Here are three university programs that could be a good fit based on your profile, focusing on your interests in Chemistry, Geography, and Computer Science, your preference for independent work, and the need for English-language instruction suitable for a Ukrainian citizen:

Wageningen University & Research (Netherlands)

+Recommended Program: BSc Environmental Sciences

Why it fits: This program strongly aligns with your interests in Chemistry and Geography. Wageningen is a top global university for environmental and life sciences. The program often involves both lab work (which can be independent) and fieldwork (addressing your dislike for purely sedentary roles). The Netherlands has support systems for Ukrainian students, and Wageningen offers some financial aid options, though specific scholarships for Ukrainians might be limited or competitive[1][2][3]. The UAF organization assists Ukrainian students seeking to study in the Netherlands[1]. Wageningen University previously offered the WURth-while project allowing refugees access to some free courses, but directs students seeking full degrees to UAF[4].

Languages of instruction: English[5].

Lund University (Sweden)

+Recommended Program: BSc Physical Geography and Ecosystem Science

Why it fits: This program integrates your interest in Geography with quantitative and computational skills (like GIS), touching upon your Computer Science interest. It focuses on environmental modelling and management[6]. Sweden generally supports Ukrainian nationals under the EU's Temporary Protection Directive, potentially exempting them from tuition fees[7]. The program emphasizes natural science foundations and includes courses in GIS and environmental modelling[6][8]. Lund University is a well-regarded institution with many English-taught programs[9][10]. Specific entry requirements include subjects like Biology, Physics, Chemistry, and Mathematics, and English proficiency (IELTS 6.5 or equivalent)[8][9][10]. Some scholarships, like the Visby Programme, have supported Ukrainian graduates in Sweden previously[11].

Languages of instruction: English[8][10].

University College London (UCL) (United Kingdom)

+Recommended Program: BSc Geography (potentially selecting the international program option or focusing on quantitative methods/GIS modules)[12][13][14]

Why it fits: UCL is a highly-ranked university offering a strong Geography program that allows specialization, including Geographic Information Science (GIS), linking your Geography and CS interests[12][14][15]. The program involves research design and can include fieldwork in the UK or abroad[12][16]. As a Ukrainian citizen potentially covered by UK government schemes (like Homes for Ukraine), you might be eligible for home fee status (£9,250/year instead of international fees, which are ~£29,400/year) and student loans[13][17][18][19]. UCL also offers student support services, including financial and immigration advice[20]. However, visa processes and living costs in London can be complex and high[13].

Languages of instruction: English[12][13].

