Advice on Next Steps

Research scholarship opportunities and specific support for Ukrainian students. Many universities and countries have specific programs, funding, or simplified admission processes for Ukrainians affected by the war[1][2][7][17][18][19][34][35][36]. Check the websites of the recommended universities (Wageningen[3][37], Lund[7], UCL[16][20]) and national resources like UAF in the Netherlands[1], the Swedish Migration Agency[7], and UKCISA/government sites for the UK[17][18][19]. Deadlines for scholarships can be early (e.g., February for some Wageningen scholarships[3][37]), so start looking now.

